"""Editorial questions for books, literature, and visual creative arts."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


BOOKS = """history_origins|How a Literary Form Developed|Which earlier texts and publishing conditions shaped one form?|Compare dated editions, manuscripts, translations, and readership records.
famous_examples|A Canonical Book Reexamined|What makes one frequently cited work distinctive in its original setting?|Read a named edition alongside contemporary reviews and later interpretations.
hidden_stories|Editors and Translators Behind a Book|Whose contribution changed a celebrated work before readers saw it?|Trace drafts, correspondence, credits, and edition variants.
beginner_explainers|How to Read a Literary Passage|How do narrator, structure, language, and context shape one passage?|Analyze a short, cited excerpt from a specified edition without universalizing an interpretation.
advanced_concepts|Voice and Unreliable Narration|What evidence in one work supports competing readings of its narrator?|Compare passages, structure, and historical reception.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Attribution|Which textual and documentary evidence bears on authorship of one work?|Assess manuscripts, publication records, stylometry limits, and alternatives.
technology_innovation|A New Book Format|How did one printing or digital technique change access and reading?|Compare production, price, preservation, and reader experience.
people_personalities|An Author's Decision in Context|What can drafts and letters establish about one revision?|Use dated primary records without treating fictional speech as autobiography.
major_events|A Publication Changes Reception|What happened after one book was released, banned, or newly translated?|Trace reviews, sales where reliable, institutions, and reader responses.
how_it_works|From Manuscript to Edition|How did author, editor, publisher, printer, and distributor shape one book?|Follow a documented edition with contracts, proofs, and physical copies.
rise_fall|A Book's Changing Readership|Why did one text gain, lose, or regain an audience?|Compare editions, curricula, libraries, adaptations, and public debate.
then_vs_now|One Text Across Editions|Which words, images, or paratext changed between two editions?|Collate named copies and explain effects on interpretation.
future_developments|A New Edition or Translation|What choices will determine whether a planned edition improves access?|Consider textual basis, translation, annotation, rights, price, and format.
myths_vs_facts|Testing a Literary Origin Story|Does a common claim about a book's inspiration appear in contemporary records?|Trace earliest attestation and compare drafts, letters, and interviews.
documentary_stories|One Book Through Its Archives|How did a work move from draft to public reception?|Build a dated chronology of manuscript, revisions, publication, and responses.
creative_brief|A Book's Stated Aim|What goal did an author or publisher set for one work?|Compare proposals, correspondence, final text, and contemporary reception.
materials_and_tools|The Physical Book as Evidence|What can paper, type, binding, or marginalia reveal about one edition?|Use catalog and conservation records for identified copies.
process_breakdown|Revision in a Manuscript|How did one scene or argument change from draft to print?|Compare dated variants and avoid claiming motive without testimony.
composition_choice|Why This Structure?|How does ordering chapters, voices, or time shape a reader's inference?|Read a named edition and compare plausible alternatives grounded in the text.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made the Published Text?|Which author, editor, translator, illustrator, or printer choices affected one edition?|Trace credit, contracts, revisions, and surviving proofs.
adaptation_across_media|A Book Becomes Another Work|Which narrative choices changed in one film, stage, or audio adaptation?|Compare scenes and medium constraints with attributed creator choices.
audience_reception|Readers Across Time|How did different readers respond to one publication?|Use dated reviews, letters, library or sales evidence, and selection limits.
cultural_context|A Work in Its Place|Which language, politics, and social debates shaped one text's publication?|Use contemporary sources without reducing the work to context alone.
preservation_restoration|Saving a Fragile Edition|What can conservators preserve and what must be documented?|Compare material condition, intervention, handling, and access policy.
rights_and_attribution|Who May Reuse the Text?|Which author, translator, illustrator, and edition rights apply to one use?|Check jurisdiction, publication date, contract, and licensed material.
style_comparison|Two Writers, One Form|How do two texts use the same formal device differently?|Compare bounded passages in original language or careful translation.
creative_failure|A Book That Missed Its Audience|Why did one publication fail to reach or persuade its intended readers?|Compare original goals, distribution, reviews, and later reassessment.
field_textual_form|Form as Meaning|How does meter, paragraph, dialogue, or typography affect one passage?|Use a named edition and show textual evidence.
field_performance_choice|A Text Read Aloud|How do two performances interpret one written passage?|Compare pacing, emphasis, translation, and the source text.
field_audience_history|Who Read It First?|What evidence describes the earliest readers of one work?|Check print runs, reviews, circulation, price, and archival bias.
field_translation_or_adaptation|A Choice in Translation|How did one translated phrase or scene alter interpretation?|Compare source text, translator note, and alternatives with linguistic context.
field_critical_reception|A Reviewer's Influence|Did one review or critical school change how a work was taught or valued?|Trace dated criticism, institutional adoption, and dissent."""


ARTS = """history_origins|An Art Practice Takes Shape|Which materials, patrons, and communities shaped one visual form?|Compare dated objects, workshop records, and attributed local histories.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Artwork Reexamined|What does one famous work reveal beyond its usual one-line interpretation?|Study material, maker, patron, original setting, and reception.
hidden_stories|Hands Behind an Artwork|Whose assistants, fabricators, suppliers, or custodians are missing from credit?|Use contracts, workshop records, technical study, and attributed voices.
beginner_explainers|Looking Closely at an Artwork|How do composition, material, scale, and setting guide one interpretation?|Use a specific object and distinguish observation from inference.
advanced_concepts|Material and Meaning|How did one material choice constrain appearance and later conservation?|Compare technical analysis, maker evidence, and environmental context.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Artist Attribution|Which evidence supports or weakens one proposed maker?|Assess provenance, signatures, materials, workshop practice, and competing views.
technology_innovation|A New Artistic Tool in Use|How did one tool alter a maker's process or audience experience?|Compare drafts, finished work, costs, and access.
people_personalities|An Artist's Choice in Context|What can notebooks, interviews, and revisions establish about one decision?|Attribute intent carefully and consider collaborators.
major_events|An Artwork Changes Hands|What happened when one object was sold, seized, donated, or returned?|Trace custody documents, claims, conservation, and affected communities.
how_it_works|From Idea to Exhibition|How did one work move through brief, making, transport, installation, and public display?|Use project records and identify each contributor.
rise_fall|A Work's Changing Reputation|Why did one artist or object move in or out of the canon?|Compare exhibitions, criticism, institutions, collecting, and excluded peers.
then_vs_now|An Artwork in Two Settings|How did location and display change how one work is seen?|Compare original context, later installation, lighting, interpretation, and access.
future_developments|A Proposed Exhibition or Restoration|What evidence should guide a planned change to one object or display?|Include condition, community consultation, access, rights, and reversibility.
myths_vs_facts|An Art Legend Checked|Does a popular story about an artwork match records?|Trace earliest version against contracts, maker notes, and provenance.
documentary_stories|An Object's Life in Records|How did one work move from making to present custody?|Build a dated sequence with gaps and disputed ownership clearly marked.
creative_brief|What Was Commissioned?|Which constraints and goals shaped one visual project?|Compare commission, sketches, budget, site, and finished result.
materials_and_tools|How Material Made the Image|Which pigments, fibers, stone, or digital tools shaped one work?|Use documented analysis and avoid unsupported material identification.
process_breakdown|A Work in Stages|What do sketches, underdrawing, or fabrication records reveal about revision?|Compare dated stages and technical evidence.
composition_choice|Why This Arrangement?|How does placement, color, scale, or perspective direct attention?|Show visible evidence and compare alternative readings.
collaborative_authorship|Artist, Workshop, and Community|Who made distinct parts of one work and how were they credited?|Use workshop records, signatures, accounts, and present stakeholder views.
adaptation_across_media|An Image in a New Medium|What changed when a visual work became print, video, or digital installation?|Compare source and adaptation, rights, material constraints, and audience.
audience_reception|How Viewers Responded|What do reviews, visitor comments, and community accounts show?|Date sources and note whose views were recorded or missing.
cultural_context|An Object's Original Use|How did one work function in its maker's community?|Use source-community accounts and period records, not only museum labels.
preservation_restoration|A Conservation Decision|Why was one treatment chosen and what evidence supports it?|Compare condition, alternatives, reversibility, and monitoring.
rights_and_attribution|Credit and Permission for an Image|Whose copyright, cultural rights, or moral rights affect reuse?|Check creator, current holder, jurisdiction, restrictions, and attribution.
style_comparison|Two Works Under One Lens|How do two makers use a shared visual device differently?|Match date, medium, purpose, and display context.
creative_failure|An Artwork's Unmet Aim|Why did one commission not achieve its intended use or reception?|Compare brief, delivery, audience evidence, and later reinterpretation.
field_visual_composition|A Detail That Changes Reading|How does one compositional feature organize meaning?|Compare close observation with maker or period evidence.
field_material_provenance|Where the Materials Came From|Can the material or object be traced through production and ownership?|Use technical study, trade records, catalog, and custody gaps.
field_maker_technique|A Technique Demonstrated|Which evidence shows how one artist made a particular effect?|Compare tool marks, technical imaging, drafts, and informed reconstruction.
field_conservation_problem|What Is Changing in the Object?|Which material deterioration threatens one artwork?|Use condition reports, environmental records, and treatment limits.
field_audience_context|Seeing Art in Place|How did audience, venue, and display conditions shape one work's reception?|Compare installation records and attributed viewer accounts."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("078", "078_books_literature", BOOKS,
                  "Books and literature through named editions, manuscripts, form, author-editor collaboration, translation, readership, rights, and preservation.",
                  "dated manuscripts and editions, author and publisher correspondence, proofs and contracts, catalog and conservation records, contemporary reviews, and attributed reader accounts",
                  "Name work, edition, language, and date. Distinguish textual evidence from author intent, identify translation choices, check rights before reproduction, and avoid unsupported single-origin stories.")
    revise_domain("079", "079_creative_arts", ARTS,
                  "Visual creative arts through material and formal choices, makers and collaborators, provenance, original use, audience reception, rights, and conservation.",
                  "identified artwork and catalog record, maker drafts and contracts, technical and condition studies, acquisition and provenance documents, contemporary criticism, and source-community accounts",
                  "Name object, maker or attribution, place, date, and custody. Attribute contested meanings and ownership, distinguish observation from inference, and check rights and community restrictions before reuse.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
